
  IPW ERL-C Version: News


Release 1.1 (1995 interim release)

  o  major problems in fpvwrite fixed -- solar radiation models now give
     correct answers, and IPW works on IBM RS/6000's now.

  o  more bugs fixed in internal libraries

  o  make now has options debug, plusdebug, and profile.

  o  txtio routines added by James Dimingo, and many QDIPS programs have
     been ported over to IPW.

  o  new programs bmask, pmask, and wigmosta to do basin masking and water
     routing.

Release 1.0

  o  ipwman now proints the author, revision date, and source at the bottom
     instead of just the revision date.  It also has a -k option, just like
     UNIX man.

  o  imtoum converts IPW manual pages into UNIX manual pages.

  o  ims uses imtoum to open pageview, ghostview, or xdvi for a nice
     manual page display.

  o  Added the option to use GNU _quicksort instead of qsort.  For some
     common inputs, Sun qsort has n squared performance which is extremely
     poor.  GNU _quicksort is much more stable.

  o  imgstat rewritten, requant replaces requantize.

  o  hdspic was renamed to ipw2hds, ipwtoppm was renamed to ipw2ppm, ipw2pgm
     was added, ipwfile was added, istatgraph was added, pbm2ipw was added.

  o  qmkhdr and stereol were removed.

  o  IPW can now write LQ headers with more than two breakpoints.

Release 0.5

  o  Testing procedures have been added for most program.  'make tests' will
     run them.

  o  A new configuration script has been added.  This automatically puts
     the configuration files into the right places given an architecture
     and an operating system.

  o  The header files are now all ANSI C compliant.  We use GNU ansidecl,
     so it will correctly handle both non-ANSI and ANSI compilers.

  o  New ANSI C error routines have been added in src/lib/libipw/error.
     These use the new stdarg interface instead of varargs, though the old
     are still supported.  stdarg is standard, varargs was a vague agreement
     that didn't always match on different operating systems.
